# Build context for web/Dockerfile, whose context is THIS directory (the app is
# self-contained: nothing in the build reads the repo root, and `pnpm build`
# never runs `tokens:check`, which is the one script that does).
#
# node_modules is the entry that matters. It is ~600 MB of pnpm store links on
# a developer's machine, it is architecture-specific (`@next/swc-*`), and the
# image installs its own from the committed lockfile — sending it would be slow
# and wrong in the same line.
node_modules
.next
out
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image, and `.env.example` is documentation the container has no
# use for. The two runtime variables are passed in, never baked (see the
# Dockerfile's header).
.env*

# Repo furniture and the editors' files: none of it is read by `next build`.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
.prettierignore
.prettierrc
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
